From 85407558a7e3aad48ca6c881fc4e44982ffea7c1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeus Dugay <duhayjeus09@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:34:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] services: add PulseCoreBridge and guard ProcessFreezerManager
 behind sysprop

- PulseCoreBridge: closed-loop ROM-to-PulseCore v0.8.0 profile sync
  (ro.pulsecore.bridge=true, opt-out persist.sys.pulsecore.auto_profile=false).
  Coordinates Battery Saver -> battery, GameSpace (ax_gaming_mode_active) ->
  gaming, unplugged screen-off -> battery (preserving full charging when
  plugged in), and interactive -> persist.sys.pulsecore.profile (default smooth).
- ProcessFreezerManager: gate behind persist.sys.process_freezer_manager
  (default true) and null-check init() in ActivityManagerService so Linux 5.4
  devices using PulseCore LaunchPulse/BinderPulse can avoid binder-freeze
  callback storms.
